rs-te-colston-loveland-season" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Where has Bears TE Colston Loveland been this season?</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-bears" data-mptype="category">Chicago Bears</a></div><span class="timestamp">4h</span><span class='author'>Courtney Cronin</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_50049468_2026-09-28T10:00:11Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="50049468" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="50049468" href="/nfl/story/_/id/50049468/chiefs-patrick-mahomes-play-action-passes-dolphins-travis-kelce-kenneth-walker-iii"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/nfl/story/_/id/50049468/chiefs-patrick-mahomes-play-action-passes-dolphins-travis-kelce-kenneth-walker-iii" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Mahomes perfect on play-action passes in win vs. Dolphins: 'It's opening up a lot'</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/kc/kansas-city-chiefs" data-mptype="category">Kansas City Chiefs</a></div><span class="timestamp">4h</span><span class='author'>Nate Taylor</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_50048227_2026-09-28T10:00:02Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="50048227" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="50048227" href="/nfl/story/_/id/50048227/joe-burrow-cincinnati-bengals-cant-close-steelers"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news"  href="/nfl/story/_/id/50048227/joe-burrow-cincinnati-bengals-cant-close-steelers" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Joe Burrow, Bengals can't 'close it out' against Steelers</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/cin/cincinnati-bengals" data-mptype="category">Cincinnati Bengals</a></div><span class="timestamp">4h</span><span class='author'>Ben Baby</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_50049013_2026-09-28T10:43:33Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="50049013" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="50049013" href="/nfl/story/_/id/50049013/cardinals-rookie-jeremiyah-love-earns-bigger-role-offense"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/nfl/story/_/id/50049013/cardinals-rookie-jeremiyah-love-earns-bigger-role-offense" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Cardinals rookie Jeremiyah Love earns bigger role in offense</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/ari/arizona-cardinals" data-mptype="category">Arizona Cardinals</a></div><span class="timestamp">12h</span><span class='author'>Josh Weinfuss</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_FFSundayHighLows-50044626_2026-09-28T04:01:44Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="FFSundayHighLows-50044626" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="FFSundayHighLows-50044626" href="/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFSundayHighLows-50044626/nfl-week-3-fantasy-football-winners-losers-injuries-rankings-more"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news"  href="/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFSundayHighLows-50044626/nfl-week-3-fantasy-football-winners-losers-injuries-rankings-more" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Week 3 winners and losers: Gibbs, Smith-Njigba stay hot; St. Brown, Taylor go quiet</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><span class="timestamp">13h</span><span class='author'>Matt Bowen and Tristan H. Cockcroft</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_40699880_2026-09-28T03:55:24Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="40699880" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="40699880" href="/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Fantasy football buzz: Top scorers through Sunday Night Football</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><span class="timestamp">10h</span><span class='author'>ESPN Fantasy</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_49745176_2026-09-28T10:00:22Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="49745176" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="49745176" href="/nfl/story/_/id/49745176/2026-nfl-playoff-predictions-afc-nfc-odds-super-bowl"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/nfl/story/_/id/49745176/2026-nfl-playoff-predictions-afc-nfc-odds-super-bowl" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">NFL playoff picture: Updated projections, chances to make the postseason</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><span class="timestamp">4h</span><span class='author'>ESPN staff</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_49794361_2026-09-28T10:00:39Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="49794361" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="49794361" href="/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49794361/2027-nfl-draft-order-projections-first-round-picks"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49794361/2027-nfl-draft-order-projections-first-round-picks" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">Projecting the 2027 NFL draft order: Which teams could have an early pick?</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/ari/arizona-cardinals" data-mptype="category">Arizona Cardinals</a></div><span class="timestamp">4h</span><span class='author'>ESPN staff</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_50046652_2026-09-28T00:08:03Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="50046652" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="50046652" href="/nfl/story/_/id/50046652/jaguars-trevor-lawrence-kneel-eight-minutes-fantasy-implications"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news"  href="/nfl/story/_/id/50046652/jaguars-trevor-lawrence-kneel-eight-minutes-fantasy-implications" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">'Give Bhayshul a touchdown.That's cool:' Trevor Lawrence explains kneel on 1</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/jax/jacksonville-jaguars" data-mptype="category">Jacksonville Jaguars</a></div><span class="timestamp">15h</span><span class='author'>Michael Dirocco</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_50046373_2026-09-28T01:02:10Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="50046373" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="50046373" href="/nfl/story/_/id/50046373/nfl-week-3-trolls-2026"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos=nfl:feed:xx:news"  href="/nfl/story/_/id/50046373/nfl-week-3-trolls-2026" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">'Rio's team now': Ravens poke fun at Cowboys after win in Rio, topping Week 3 trolls</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-commanders" data-mptype="category">Washington Commanders</a></div><span class="timestamp">14h</span><span class='author'>Anthony Gharib</span></div></div></div></div><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_49466506_2026-09-28T12:44:51Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="49466506" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="49466506" href="/espn/betting/story/_/id/49466506/nfl-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/espn/betting/story/_/id/49466506/nfl-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">NFL betting buzz: 8.5 the magic number for underdogs</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/nfl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-seahawks" data-mptype="category">Seattle Seahawks</a></div><span class="timestamp">8d</span><span class='author'>ESPN</span></div></div></div></div><!--set: espn-en_story_nfl_50048459_2026-09-28T03:49:22Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><!--set: espn-en_story_nfl_50048829_2026-09-28T13:36:23Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><!--get: espn-en_story_nfl_49881131_2026-09-27T16:36:59Z_false_false_desktop_full_11--><div data-id="49881131" class="news-feed-item "><a name="&lpos=" class="story-link"   data-sport="nfl" data-id="49881131" href="/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49881131/2027-nfl-draft-risers-questions-college-football-prospects"></a><div class="text-container"><div class="item-info-wrap"><div class="news-feed-item-title"><a name="&lpos="  href="/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49881131/2027-nfl-draft-risers-questions-college-football-prospects" class="realStory" data-sport="nfl">NFL draft risers, notes off Saturday's college games: Is Colin Simmons the class's clear top edge rusher?</a></div><div class="news-feed_item-meta "><div class="category-link"><a href="/college-football/team/_/id/251/texas-longhorns" data-mptype="category">Texas Longhorns</a></div><span class="timestamp">22h</span><span class='author'>Mel Kiper Jr. and Jordan Reid</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="article-feed" class="col-b" data-behavior="author_overlay article_header_news_feed_item_meta article_legal_footer"><article class="article" data-id="50043408" data-behavior="story_scroll story_progress byline_lines iframe" data-src="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026"><div class="container"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-instream ad-wrapper" data-slot-type="instream" data-slot-kvps="pos=instream"></div><header class="article-header"><h1>NFL Week 3: Takeaways, questions, fantasy spin for Sunday's games</h1></header><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50049788" data-cerebro-id="6ab9e72d75ba89659fc67895" data-title="Broncos pick off Stafford on final play to seal win over Rams" class="iframe-video article-figure video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><div class="img-wrap"><picture ><source srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0928/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0928/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0928/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25/4de67e1575a3416ab1376a7be662428d25.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  data-image-container=".article-figure" ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50049788">play</span></div><figcaption><div class="caption-wrapper"><div class="text-container"><span class="headline">Broncos pick off Stafford on final play to seal win over Rams (0:31)</span><p></p></div></div></figcaption></figure><div class="article-body"><div class="article-meta"><div class="byline-wrap"><ul class="authors byline-authors"><li class="single-author mugshot-shown"><div class="author-img"><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/columnists/espn_generic_m.jpg&h=80&w=80&scale=crop" alt="" width="40" height="40"></div><div class="author has-bio">NFL Nation<span class="timestamp ">Sep 28, 2026, 12:27 AM ET</span></div><div class="author-overlay"><a class="icon-font-after icon-close-solid-after" href="#">Close</a><ul>NFL Nation is made up of 32 team-specific reporters who cover the NFL year-round across ESPN.com, ESPN television shows, ESPN Radio, ESPN+ and social media platforms. It was established ahead of the 2013 season.</ul><div class="author-meta"></div></div></li></ul><div class="byline-multiple-authors" style="display:none;">Multiple Authors</div></div></div><div class="content-reactions reactions-allowed " data-behavior="content_reactions" data-contentid="50043408" data-nowid="1-50043408" data-contentTitle="NFL Week 3: Takeaways, questions, fantasy spin for Sunday's games"><div class="content-reactions-popup-overlay"></div><div class="content-reactions_reactions-wrapper"><div class="share-button-wrapper"><button class="icon-button reactions-button reactions-hover-button share-button user-not-parsed" data-behavior="share_button" aria-label="Share"></button><div class="share-popup"><ul class="share-popup-list social-tracking-parent" data-id="50043408" data-name="NFL Week 3: Takeaways, questions, fantasy spin for Sunday's games" data-type="article"><li><a data-behavior="copy_link" data-social-tool="copy" href="#" data-social-type="content" class="share-popup-link icon-font-before icon-chain-solid-before reactions-copy-link copy-link" aria-label="Copy Link"><span class="copy-link-inner"><span class="copy-link-inner-text share__label"></span><span class="copy-link-success-icon"><img class="icon" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/content-reactions/check.png&h=80&w=80" alt="Copy Link" loading="lazy"></span></span></a></li><li><a data-social-tool="email" href="mailto:?subject=NFL%20Week%203%3A%20Takeaways,%20questions,%20fantasy%20spin%20for%20Sunday%27s%20games&body=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.espn.com%2Fnfl%2Fstory%2F_%2Fid%2F50043408" data-social-type="content" class="share-popup-link icon-font-before icon-email-solid-before email social-clicks-email" aria-label="Email">Email</a></li><li><a data-social-tool="print" href="https://www.espn.com/espn/print?id=50043408" data-social-type="content" class="share-popup-link print icon-font-before icon-print-solid-before page-action" aria-label="Print">Print</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="content-reactions-extended-wrapper"><button class="icon-button reactions-button main-reactions-button reactions-hover-button"></button><button class="sr-only main-reactions-sr-only">Open Extended Reactions</button><div class="main-reactions-popup content-reactions-popup"></div></div></div><div class="content-reactions_count-wrapper"><button class="icon-button reactions-button reactions-count-button reactions-hover-button" data-native-bridge="true"></button><div class="reactions-count-popup content-reactions-popup"></div></div><div class="reactions-skeleton-loading"><div class="reactions-skeleton-left"><div class="reactions-skeleton-el share-skeleton"></div><div class="reactions-skeleton-el"></div></div><div class="reactions-skeleton-right"><div class="reactions-skeleton-el"></div></div></div></div><p>Week 3 of the <a href="/nfl/schedule">2026 NFL season</a> featured shocking performances in the early window Sunday, including another turnover-filled afternoon by Patriots quarterback <a data-player-guid="2fbd2f9e-624d-3e63-9bb5-9bb965782b68" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431452/drake-maye">Drake Maye</a> and a three-touchdown performance by Lions running back <a data-player-guid="d85aed19-e3b8-3788-935e-55f636ad86e9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429795/jahmyr-gibbs">Jahmyr Gibbs</a>. Commanders backup quarterback <a data-player-guid="33be1f4a-d812-75b9-7b7c-5319d2a7113a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota">Marcus Mariota</a> also led the team to a huge upset over the Seahawks.</p><p>Elsewhere during the early window, the Steelers got the best of a shootout versus the Bengals. The Giants defeated the Titans without starting quarterback <a data-player-guid="13e97d3e-2171-371b-9a7a-2c44670b5a62" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4689114/jaxson-dart">Jaxson Dart</a>, while the Browns won their second straight game.</p><p>The late window was filled with close games, with all four contests separated by a touchdown at the start of the fourth quarter. The Ravens-Cowboys matchup was the most exciting of the bunch in Rio de Janeiro, ending on a time-expiring, winning field goal by Baltimore's <a data-player-guid="16f0a87e-34cf-34ca-ad36-1c2245aa36e9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4697745/tyler-loop">Tyler Loop</a>. The Sunday night game was a classic, with the Broncos overcoming a 16-point halftime deficit to stun the Rams in the final minute in Denver.</p><p>Our NFL Nation reporters reacted to all the action, answering lingering questions coming out of each game and detailing everything else you need to know for teams that played Sunday. Fantasy football analysts Matt Bowen and Tristan Cockcroft also have fantasy takeaways from each matchup. Let's get to it.</p><p align="center"><strong>Jump to:</strong><br />
<a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#larden">LAR-DEN</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#dalbal">BAL-DAL</a><br />
 <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#lvno">LV-NO</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#mintb">MIN-TB</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#arisf">ARI-SF</a><br />
<a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#seawsh">SEA-WSH</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#carcle">CAR-CLE</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#cinpit">CIN-PIT</a><br />
<a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#tennyg">TEN-NYG</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#lacbuf">LAC-BUF</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#houind">HOU-IND</a><br />
<a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#nyjdet">NYJ-DET</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#nejax">NE-JAX</a> | <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026#kcmia">KC-MIA</a></p><p align="center"><strong>Catch up on Thursday's game:</strong><br />
<a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50023295/nfl-green-bay-packers-atlanta-falcons-jordan-love-michael-penix">ATL-GB</a></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="larden"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872962">Denver 30, L.A. Rams 26</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872962">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872962">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/den.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Broncos</h2><p><strong>Another wild comeback in the books, but can the Broncos continue to survive their chronic slow starts?</strong> The Broncos are 2-1 despite the first halves of their first three games being an exercise in offensive pain. The Broncos were held scoreless in the first two quarters Sunday night and have scored only 10 first-half points this season. The defense held Los Angeles to 1-of-3 in the red zone in the first two quarters, keeping the Broncos close enough for a second-half offensive surge. All-Pro safety <a data-player-guid="379f2aa6-c5f8-b840-c0e3-e7f8ef5a8d2b" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360853/talanoa-hufanga" target="_new">Talanoa Hufanga</a> had two interceptions, a pick-six and the game-sealing pick on the final play, but this penchant for close calls might come back to haunt Denver.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> <a data-player-guid="f9de7512-a950-3317-816b-abe094068409" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426338/bo-nix" target="_new">Bo Nix</a> continues to show two personalities. He was out of sorts in the first half, completing 6 of 12 passes for 53 yards and nearly threw an interception. Same quarterback, different story in the second half. Nix once again bounced back despite a second-half interception. The Broncos scored on two of their first three possessions of the second half to tie the score after trailing by 16 points, and Nix led Denver to the winning score with 47 seconds left, capping a 65-yard drive with a 1-yard QB sneak for a touchdown. <em>-- Jeff Legwold</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at 49ers (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/lar.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Rams</h2><p><strong>Will Puka Nacua's return fix the Rams' red zone woes?</strong> The Rams' offense moved the ball well in the first half against the Broncos, gaining 273 yards, but struggled to convert in the red zone. The Rams were 1-of-4 in the red zone Sunday, with the lone score coming on a 5-yard touchdown pass from <a data-player-guid="20c41c33-a33f-6dc2-7e1f-0771e39ce49a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/12483/matthew-stafford" target="_new">Matthew Stafford</a> to tight end <a data-player-guid="93f414a4-0330-7851-b0e0-752bbd975157" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2573401/tyler-higbee" target="_new">Tyler Higbee</a> near the end of the first quarter. On the other two drives, the Rams had to settle for field goals. Nacua has missed the past two games but is expected to be back for Week 4 against the Eagles.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> In the first half, <a data-player-guid="d287bc03-47c2-c7f6-6160-e4280c80d2e2" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16800/davante-adams" target="_new">Davante Adams</a> had four catches for 71 yards on five targets when matched up against Broncos cornerback <a data-player-guid="1e86c395-b340-8084-cacb-61d1eb0fa424" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4372012/pat-surtain-ii" target="_new">Pat Surtain II</a>, whom Adams called "one of the best DBs in the league." Adams gained 71 yards in the first half, the most Surtain has given up before halftime in his career, according to ESPN Research. Adams finished the game with seven catches for 137 yards. <em>-- Sarah Barshop</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Eagles (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> <a data-player-guid="f22d9167-1359-d2cc-4c4d-b31ab83ad48d" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430737/kyren-williams" target="_new">Kyren Williams</a> has had back-to-back games with 34 more rushing yards than expected and at least 15 fantasy points, strengthening his role as the Rams' primary back after <a data-player-guid="cf0a37e4-de10-3077-b71b-0f06a27d0ff1" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429096/blake-corum" target="_new">Blake Corum</a> totaled 22 carries in Weeks 1-2. Williams remains a weekly fantasy RB2, even with the Eagles up next. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="dalbal"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872960">Baltimore 34, Dallas 31</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872960">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872960">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/bal.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Ravens</h2><p><strong>Did the Ravens exorcise their penchant for fourth-quarter collapses?</strong> <a data-player-guid="7d76fbb1-1c5e-d9f4-954f-cad43f720ae2" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3916387/lamar-jackson">Lamar Jackson</a> and the Ravens gave an authoritative response to the "same old Ravens" narrative. <a data-player-guid="16f0a87e-34cf-34ca-ad36-1c2245aa36e9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4697745/tyler-loop">Tyler Loop</a>'s 56-yard field goal with no time remaining lifted Baltimore to an improbable comeback. With seven seconds remaining, Jackson completed a 26-yard pass to wide receiver <a data-player-guid="04e6bfd5-ecba-2d02-bcac-087f32564877" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429615/zay-flowers">Zay Flowers</a>, who was a game-time decision because of a <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50044202/ravens-flowers-play-having-positive-rio-workout-source-says">hamstring injury</a>. It was redemption for Loop, whose errant 44-yard field goal attempt ended Baltimore's playoff hopes last season. Over the past six seasons, the Ravens have lost an NFL-worst 15 games when leading through three quarters. But they found a way to win Sunday.</p><p><strong>Stat to know:</strong> With two touchdowns, running back <a data-player-guid="81c182a5-8981-2272-a00f-f8daf9533e07" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3043078/derrick-henry">Derrick Henry</a> became the oldest player (32 years, 166 days) in NFL history to score six touchdowns in the first three games of a season. His 34 career games with multiple rushing touchdowns are the most among active players -- 16 more than the next-closest players (<a data-player-guid="a83b6715-f018-aedf-190e-f77f026c7e4a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4047365/josh-jacobs">Josh Jacobs</a> and <a data-player-guid="ddd8786c-fd5a-4e55-ccc8-6ddf6f1ede33" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4242335/jonathan-taylor">Jonathan Taylor</a> with 18). <em>-- Jamison Hensley</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Titans (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50047977" data-cerebro-id="6ab9acff4bf4c005207bb814" data-title="What a finish! Ravens down Cowboys in Brazil with wild ending sequence" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220/9f0d444ef845490a8fa5aa7f16edb7f91220.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50047977">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:52</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">What a finish! Ravens down Cowboys in Brazil with wild ending sequence</div></div></div><hr><p><alsoee></alsoee></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/dal.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Cowboys</h2><p><strong>Is this any different than the Cowboys' past two seasons?</strong> The Cowboys showed moxie to come back from an 11-point deficit, but ultimately, couldn't hold on. Why? A defense that was worn down and worn out. With 7:29 left, the offense had a chance to run down the clock but held the ball for only 1:44. Similar to 2024 and 2025, the Cowboys are 1-2 after two games. The comeback showed some fight, but now they won't get back to work until Tuesday due to traveling back from Brazil. Can Brian Schottenheimer's team make sure this isn't a repeat of the past two seasons, when they finished 7-10 and 7-9-1?</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> The Cowboys are supposed to have a big-play offense, but <a data-player-guid="5f09781b-6b0b-7325-049b-a91e60d794e6" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2577417/dak-prescott">Dak Prescott</a> did not have a completion of more than 13 yards until the third quarter. On the go-ahead drive, he hit <a data-player-guid="2994891b-8927-33cb-6999-e809560d0545" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4241389/ceedee-lamb">CeeDee Lamb</a> for a 49-yard bomb from the Dallas 6-yard line. Before the completion to Lamb, Prescott had just one attempt of 20 or more yards and was attempting just 6.2 air yards per attempt. He averaged 7.4 in Weeks 1-2. <em>-- Todd Archer</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Texans (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Ravens backup TE <a data-player-guid="21f4d071-73c2-3b82-8c0d-3adf08c9b376" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432260/matthew-hibner">Matthew Hibner</a> caught both of his targets for 23 yards and a touchdown (10.3 fantasy points) on an end zone throw from Jackson. Hibner has run a total of only 23 routes over his first three games, but he projects as a potential insurance policy for starter <a data-player-guid="eb0163cd-c488-df37-0418-93144048fba1" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3116365/mark-andrews">Mark Andrews</a>, who briefly left the game because of a hand injury. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="lvno"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872961">Las Vegas 35, New Orleans 27</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872961">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872961">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/lv.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Raiders</h2><p><strong>With <a data-player-guid="53bec012-c2ed-bc7c-a8d5-438611f9faa1" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/14880/kirk-cousins">Kirk Cousins</a> playing well, will <a data-player-guid="2d69f2b3-fc07-332b-bd84-8793a3a1b74a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4837248/fernando-mendoza">Fernando Mendoza</a> have to wait longer than expected?</strong> The Raiders know Mendoza's time to be the starter is looming, but he might have to wait a little longer. Cousins has the Raiders at 3-0 and has played well. Against the Saints, Cousins completed 22 of 33 passes for 248 yards and three touchdowns. He has thrown nine touchdowns in three games, and the team has fully embraced him as a leader. There's still no need to rush Mendoza on the field.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> Las Vegas scored 30-plus points in a game for the first time since its <a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401547593/chargers-raiders">63-21 win</a> over the Chargers in Week 15 of 2023. The Raiders have scored at least 25 points in three straight contests. The Raiders scored more than 25 points only once during the 2025 campaign under former coach Pete Carroll.</p><p><b>Best quote from the locker room:</b> "It's a 17-game season, so we can't be happy or satisfied with this win," Raiders coach Klint Kubiak said. "Put ourselves in a good position. We know what's coming to our place next week: the Chiefs. So we just take it one game at a time. That's how you win games."<em>-- Ryan McFadden</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Chiefs (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50047882" data-cerebro-id="6ab9ab1df340d6751fab3802" data-title="Brock Bowers' TD extends the Raiders' lead" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60/08a60e93-27a6-4a73-8a9c-12ed4064ae60.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50047882">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:41</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Brock Bowers' TD extends the Raiders' lead</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/no.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Saints</h2><p><strong>What went wrong late for the Saints?</strong> Multiple turnovers were an issue in the second half. The Saints were playing backup left tackle <a data-player-guid="abc40df5-6261-dc03-24cd-a623ae477711" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430379/asim-richards">Asim Richards</a> because <a data-player-guid="373f5426-76be-3f60-84dd-e3827fc3fd93" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685260/kelvin-banks-jr">Kelvin Banks Jr</a>. was on injured reserve, and Richards gave up a sack that led to a fumble and points for Las Vegas. Later, Richards was backed into <a data-player-guid="0eb2837a-e6ed-bbd7-d7d5-cbeb2cd7ab11" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360689/tyler-shough">Tyler Shough</a>, who threw a wobbly interception as a result. The Raiders took the lead by scoring quickly afterward. The Saints had a chance to drive downfield and try to tie the score twice, but they turned the ball over -- again.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> Shough was cooking until two fourth-quarter turnovers. The second-year QB showed an ability to move the offense at a level not seen in New Orleans in years. But Shough, who was making his 12th start, showed he still has some growing to do. Also, the Saints will have to get better about protecting their QB in key moments.</p><p><b>Best quote from the locker room:</b> "Yeah, I don't know. I mean, there was just no flow to that game," Saints coach Kellen Moore commented on what <a data-player-guid="d0d41d17-2f81-391d-bddd-8375526f71ff" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4683215/danny-stutsman" target="_new">Danny Stutsman</a> should have done differently on a roughing the passer penalty that led to a Raiders second-quarter touchdown.<em>-- Katherine Terrell</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Falcons (Monday, 8:15 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Forgive him for the two tough losses in three weeks, but the Saints' Shough has been outstanding operating in Kellen Moore's offense thus far. Shough has exceeded 22 fantasy points in all three games, is making good use of his receivers and is showing strong mobility. He has arrived as a matchup-dependent QB1. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="mintb"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872959">Minnesota 23, Tampa Bay 16</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872959">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872959">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/min.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Vikings</h2><p><strong>Can WR <a data-player-guid="7e13f346-0248-31d6-a4e7-8467003d0f8b" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429205/jordan-addison">Jordan Addison</a> fill in for <a data-player-guid="c7fb1996-2530-7f98-9f2f-572debf989f4" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4262921/justin-jefferson">Justin Jefferson</a>?</strong> Nope. And that's not intended to be a knock on Addison, who is a very talented WR2. But Jefferson, who left in the first quarter because of an ankle injury, is one of the best players in the NFL. Addison made several acrobatic catches, including a 30-yard reception along the sideline and a 41-yard touchdown. But to this point in his career, he has not been a receiver around whom opponents need to design their game plan.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> <a data-player-guid="9bef707d-d33f-266b-3020-81900d735915" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917315/kyler-murray">Kyler Murray</a>'s first full game of his Vikings tenure was rocky to say the least. He found Addison on those two big plays, but otherwise, the Vikings couldn't move the ball after Jefferson departed. At one point, Murray completed only 2 of 15 passes. The Vikings barely had more first downs (nine) than punts (eight). <em>-- Kevin Seifert</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Dolphins (Sunday, 4:05 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50046929" data-cerebro-id="6ab99926f340d6751fab3137" data-title="Kyler Murray throws a 41-yard touchdown pass to Jordan Addison" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c/64d96666-a5fc-4baf-85e1-04503bac919c.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50046929">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:40</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Kyler Murray throws a 41-yard touchdown pass to Jordan Addison</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/tb.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Buccaneers</h2><p><strong>Is there any hope of this getting better?</strong> The defense holding a Jefferson-less Vikings to six points in the second half gave the Bucs a chance, but what the offense is doing is unsustainable. Quarterback <a data-player-guid="5bb4376a-d089-e3e4-e49a-44f1d709a012" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3052587/baker-mayfield">Baker Mayfield</a>, who missed the final drive after injuring his thumb and finished 17-of-34 for 217 passing yards, was sacked six times, and the offense went just 2-of-17 on third down. That made it incredibly difficult to climb out of a 10-0 hole.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> The Mayfield-to-<a data-player-guid="fcb8cea5-a51b-3b85-93fa-0f934f6e60ef" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5220680/ted-hurst">Ted Hurst III</a> connection showed improvement with a 40-yard touchdown in the first quarter, but a <a data-player-guid="c4a26a1b-f10a-dfe1-466f-29f16b7226a5" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4380507/luke-goedeke">Luke Goedeke</a> holding call wiped out <a data-player-guid="20e1bec6-fb6a-9ab1-92e0-c13eff7a7d42" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3116165/chris-godwin-jr">Chris Godwin Jr</a>.'s would-be score later on. And, of course, there was that fourth-quarter interception, which brought Mayfield's turnover total to five this season. <em>-- Jenna Laine</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Packers (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway: </strong>Addison's 20.0-fantasy-point performance aside, Buccaneers WR <a data-player-guid="48fb595b-ecda-3de2-9c05-fcc8090c4b84" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4567750/emeka-egbuka">Emeka Egbuka</a>'s managers must hope that Mayfield's thumb injury doesn't sideline him long term. Egbuka hasn't hit his ceiling -- one he did often in the early stages of 2025 -- and he'd have a tougher time being a weekly WR2 with rookie <a data-player-guid="aaab6e81-bfa6-3ceb-bb91-e9e31a23552b" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4596472/jalon-daniels">Jalon Daniels</a> as his QB. -- Cockcroft</p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="arisf"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872958">San Francisco 36, Arizona 30</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872958">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872958">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/sf.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>49ers</h2><p><strong>How much longer can the 49ers withstand all of the injuries?</strong> Perhaps no team in the league is more accustomed to fighting through significant injuries than the 49ers, but even they can withstand only so much. They eked out a win despite losing WR <a data-player-guid="5073fc58-91c1-4e3d-826d-af754f9f40c7" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16737/mike-evans">Mike Evans</a> (ribs), LT <a data-player-guid="569156ee-309b-ce78-c1ac-1e9494943ce2" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/13241/trent-williams">Trent Williams</a> (stinger) and LB <a data-player-guid="22bed4b5-a5ad-ccac-e96e-4ba5bd7d1173" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3916903/dre-greenlaw">Dre Greenlaw</a> (quad) -- on top of the many players the 49ers were missing entering the game. The schedule gets tougher from here, starting with matchups against Denver and Seattle. <a data-player-guid="d2e39a38-732d-5a24-f242-a4f9de87dabe" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361741/brock-purdy">Brock Purdy</a> is playing as well as any quarterback in the league, and that effort has the Niners at 3-0, but Purdy must continue to perform for them to keep rolling.</p><p><strong>Most surprising performance:</strong> Second-year WR <a data-player-guid="280e4563-f82e-37a3-a9ea-fd1a0232346f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431466/jordan-watkins">Jordan Watkins</a> had not played this season and entered Sunday's game with two catches for 26 yards in his career. But with Evans departing the game in the second quarter, Watkins got his opportunity. He had two catches for 60 yards, including a 34-yard catch to set up <a data-player-guid="4b504ee0-cda2-d632-1bc0-2da4344d7bde" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4034949/eddy-pineiro">Eddy Pineiro</a>'s 57-yard field goal at the end of the first half.</p><p><b>Best quote from the locker room:</b> Tight end <a data-player-guid="9c61fb91-fc5a-7cc3-8367-a8dbc589f97a" href="http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle" target="_new">George Kittle</a> on the need of the 49ers' offense to carry the freight with so many injuries decimating the defense, especially on the line: "The NFL is hard to get wins in. With our offense, with coach Shanahan and with <a data-player-guid="d2e39a38-732d-5a24-f242-a4f9de87dabe" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361741/brock-purdy" target="_new">Brock Purdy</a> at the helm, we need to put up points. And we have enough guys out there regardless of who's on the field, to score points, especially with Brock throwing the ball and Christian running it."<em>-- Nick Wagoner</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Broncos (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50047725" data-cerebro-id="6ab9a4a875ba89659fc649df" data-title="George Kittle cushions the 49ers' lead with a TD from Brock Purdy" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166/f754dc8fe9be4938a0df50a43e2cd9e91166.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50047725">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:31</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">George Kittle cushions the 49ers' lead with a TD from Brock Purdy</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/ari.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Cardinals</h2><p><strong>How can the Cardinals' second-half offensive showing springboard them forward?</strong> Even in a loss, Arizona looked like a team that could score on anyone in the second half after scoring just six pints in the first half. Even though the 49ers were trying to keep the Cardinals' playmakers in front of them, they used a mix of short passes and the run to open medium and long passes. That turned a potential blowout into a close game.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> Eight. That's the number of penalties the Cardinals had in the first half, hampering offensive progress throughout the first two quarters. The Cardinals had just two in the second half, a telling difference . <em>-- Josh Weinfuss</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Giants (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> If the 49ers' Evans misses time, managers should bump up TE <a data-player-guid="9c61fb91-fc5a-7cc3-8367-a8dbc589f97a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle">George Kittle</a> and WR <a data-player-guid="7f300cb7-f0a1-a43a-d0b0-f8a57bf04eb3" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3126486/deebo-samuel-sr">Deebo Samuel Sr</a>. as priority targets in the route tree. Plus, the receiving usage for RB <a data-player-guid="db08ac19-dbd9-a776-5885-de1fe6830bc2" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117251/christian-mccaffrey">Christian McCaffrey</a> (flexed from the formation) could increase, which opens the door for rookie RB <a data-player-guid="18da8955-6970-39eb-bc40-a716f476a1d3" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4696044/kaelon-black">Kaelon Black</a> to see more carries. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="seawsh"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872955">Washington 33, Seattle 31</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872955">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872955">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/wsh.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Commanders</h2><p><strong>How did this happen?</strong> Turnovers and an efficient offense. The Commanders forced three turnovers, leading to three touchdowns -- two by the offense and another on a pick-six by linebacker <a data-player-guid="4a393e3c-e035-528c-3ec5-6c22d690a37c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4427984/kain-medrano">Kain Medrano</a>. The offense capitalized on two short fields after a fumble and an interception, while quarterback <a data-player-guid="33be1f4a-d812-75b9-7b7c-5319d2a7113a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota">Marcus Mariota</a> did what was needed. He was smart with the ball, making quick throws and taking checkdowns to keep the chains moving. And he was aggressive when necessary, like on a tight-window throw to WR Trey Burks for his second touchdown. It was an unlikely win without quarterback <a data-player-guid="f03f3238-b035-6f0e-5844-1529ca021c3a" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426348/jayden-daniels">Jayden Daniels</a>, linebacker <a data-player-guid="2a6c9a31-1755-da1d-6071-0e3389949107" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3127273/frankie-luvu">Frankie Luvu</a>, tight end <a data-player-guid="eb564484-2114-ece2-1581-1bf179af62c8" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360635/chig-okonkwo">Chig Okonkwo</a>, right guard <a data-player-guid="5ed1f0d9-1930-0aa5-4c0f-81f78ff4dedb" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4262199/sam-cosmi">Sam Cosmi</a> and safety <a data-player-guid="128929e5-654a-69c4-c16e-a3d2a0c20dff" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426403/nick-cross">Nick Cross</a>.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Washington did not force any turnovers in its first two games, which continued an ugly trend: Only one team has forced fewer turnovers than the Commanders since 2024. But they harped on it all offseason, and the focus paid off Sunday. Can they sustain it? It helped that they played coverage much better than they did against Dallas in Week 2. But to get more, the front needs to generate more consistent pressure. It'll help when they get blitzing linebacker Frankie Luvu back soon from a groin injury. <em>-- John Keim</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Colts in London (Sunday, 9:30 a.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50045227" data-cerebro-id="6ab97b55f340d6751fab1d19" data-title="Kain Medrano comes up with clutch pick-six for Commanders" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998/0b67a630009b482aa0e8bc6481c67658998.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50045227">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:48</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Kain Medrano comes up with clutch pick-six for Commanders</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/sea.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Seahawks</h2><p><strong>What was most concerning about Seattle's upset loss?</strong> The defending Super Bowl champions came into this game on a 12-game winning streak, with <a data-player-guid="938f19a1-ef9b-618c-2365-d55291e0fcc6" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3912547/sam-darnold">Sam Darnold</a> back at quarterback, and as the much healthier team. There were plenty of reasons they lost as 8.5-point favorites, but a big one was their absence of a run game -- something they could have used in the rain. Seattle's tailbacks gained just 39 yards on 17 carries. Rookie <a data-player-guid="705bfe8e-8678-32bc-a5b8-535fcca2e1cd" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685512/jadarian-price">Jadarian Price</a> lost his second fumble in as many weeks to set up Washington's first touchdown. The Seahawks got away with turnovers last season because their defense and special teams were so good. But they didn't do enough to overcome three giveaways against Washington.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> Darnold's return from the glute injury that sidelined him for most of the first two games was a mixed bag. With no run game, he carried the offense by completing 31 of 45 attempts for 379 yards, four touchdowns and two interceptions -- one coming on a throw that was deflected at the line of scrimmage, while the other was a back-breaking pick-six in the fourth quarter. Two of Darnold's TD passes were to <a data-player-guid="edf87204-0e8c-331c-ac63-c6e04a89ee76" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430878/jaxon-smith-njigba">Jaxon Smith-Njigba</a>, but he spread the ball around more than <a data-player-guid="0b8ae860-a909-6cdb-db2d-8e3fe1b28d83" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3924327/drew-lock">Drew Lock</a> did.</p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Chargers (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room:</strong> On his pick-six, Darnold was trying to find tight end <a data-player-guid="63c4b629-3362-32db-b424-d0f9201c846f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4576297/aj-barner">AJ Barner</a>, but defensive end <a data-player-guid="3abbb66c-4907-9b5f-08cd-19b5d7914c6e" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361422/odafe-oweh">Odafe Oweh</a> kept him in the pocket, and Medrano jumped the short, play-action throw over the middle. "Just a bad decision," Darnold said. "The end did a good job of not letting me escape to the outside and I had to make a quick decision and I should have dirted it at his feet. ... I saw him. He made a really good play, but that's a ball I've got to throw away." <em>-- Brady Henderson</em></p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Commanders WR <a data-player-guid="04454e17-9294-6271-f951-c0339528e97e" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3121422/terry-mclaurin">Terry McLaurin</a> caught six of a team-high nine targets from Marcus Mariota, finishing with 77 yards and a touchdown (19.7 fantasy points). With this type of volume -- and clear on-field chemistry with Mariota -- McLaurin fits as a WR2/flex option for Week 4. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="carcle"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872949">Cleveland 21, Carolina 18</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872949">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872949">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/cle.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Browns</h2><p><strong>Is <a data-player-guid="b6ec8e9e-3d85-a1de-9d0a-5a51621a9c20" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3122840/deshaun-watson">Deshaun Watson</a> turning the corner?</strong> For the second straight week, Watson engineered a game-winning touchdown drive. This time, it helped turn around a slow start for the Browns' offense that lasted three quarters. Entering the fourth quarter, Watson was 10-for-21 for 67 yards and a touchdown. However, he has been at his best when the Browns have needed it the most. On the game-winning drive, Watson converted a pair of third downs, including his touchdown.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> Defensive tackle <a data-player-guid="9167867c-52d4-3d9e-982c-f4b7ad9f259b" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4873232/mason-graham">Mason Graham</a> recorded his fourth sack in three games (two on Sunday against <a data-player-guid="975cc6da-01e5-3dcc-8a1a-1c9ecdb27d58" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685720/bryce-young">Bryce Young</a>). That made him the first Browns player since <a data-player-guid="031d8156-6271-ea30-409f-137309621805" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3122132/myles-garrett">Myles Garrett</a> in 2019 to record a sack in the first three games of the season. Graham had a half-sack throughout all of last season as a rookie.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room: </strong>"We're playing for first place. Holy s---! Is that cool or what? Our guys are ready to rock and roll and we'll be good to go," coach Todd Monken exclaimed after Sunday's win. "But appreciate the fans and we're not perfect. We're not coaching or playing. We're going to fight like hell to get there, I promise." <em>-- Daniel Oyefusi</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Steelers (Thursday, 8:15 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50045467" data-cerebro-id="6ab97d87f340d6751fab1da2" data-title="Deshaun Watson finds Harold Fannin Jr. for late TD to give Browns the lead" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/0927/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006/cc63c38f80a542f88eb27ba9a914dde71006.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50045467">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:39</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Deshaun Watson finds Harold Fannin Jr. for late TD to give Browns the lead</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/car.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Panthers</h2><p><strong>Is this offensive line sustainable until <a data-player-guid="a9d960e7-140d-ed68-d984-7f0622735ae8" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2973051/taylor-moton">Taylor Moton</a> and <a data-player-guid="73e3d8e5-b2bd-bdae-11a3-dcaf7a35e458" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4427132/ikem-ekwonu">Ikem Ekwonu</a> return from their respective injuries?</strong> The Panthers have struggled to run the ball efficiently through three weeks. Carolina's ground attack was stifled Sunday, as running back <a data-player-guid="7c6b0551-49b5-aa13-9e26-7db2f9dad46f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4241416/chuba-hubbard">Chuba Hubbard</a> produced 18 yards on 10 carries in the first half; he still finished with 82 rushing yards on 19 carries. With left guard <a data-player-guid="5fad68ec-cc68-6b5d-7d35-d727ad902598" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4362647/damien-lewis">Damien Lewis</a> forced from the game for a stretch, the line leaned on backup <a data-player-guid="b8d4e4a0-a9e4-b966-a681-7f2e4994e2c9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4576075/corey-bullock">Corey Bullock</a>, who didn't improve matters during his brief playing time. In addition, QB Bryce Young was sacked twice before halftime.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> While Young led five scoring drives, his aerial attack was subdued by the Browns. He was erratic with a crowded pocket, and he benefited from a pair of roughing the passer penalties on the final drive of the first half to put points on the board. Young finished with 291 passing yards, a TD and an INT.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room:</strong> "I think we all just got to do a better job. I think we're just kind of -- I hate to say it -- one man off every time. That could be from me or anybody else," said Panthers right guard <a data-player-guid="bf60bbda-b870-32c6-9003-cddb87945c73" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2138951/rob-hunt">Rob Hunt</a> of the team's run game struggles. "So we've just got to be on the same page. I think we've just got to click, and I think later in the game, it felt good and it looked good. We've got to start early. If we start early, it's a different ball game."<em> -- Mike Kaye</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Lions (Sunday, 8:20 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Browns rookie WR <a data-player-guid="1cb83812-2715-3ded-bb86-4c276fc0060c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4832800/denzel-boston">Denzel Boston</a> was a priority waiver wire add after catching a touchdown in each of his first two games. In Sunday's win, he caught only two of four targets for 41 yards (8.1 points). Boston has the explosive play ability to post a big number in the lineup, but he should be viewed as a boom/bust WR3 in a very inconsistent offense. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="cinpit"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872950">Pittsburgh 30, Cincinnati 27</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872950">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872950">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/pit.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Steelers</h2><p><strong>How has CB <a data-player-guid="947fca04-4472-9b5d-251a-3cdd97841e20" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426506/joey-porter-jr">Joey Porter Jr</a>.'s absence impacted the Steelers?</strong> Porter was inactive for a third week in a row as he continues to "ramp up" amid his aggravated back injury and contentious contract situation. Bengals QB <a data-player-guid="e6957db5-5b2e-a82d-c788-d889115d9772" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3915511/joe-burrow">Joe Burrow</a> picked on CB <a data-player-guid="d3e870a4-6ef6-23a2-d633-1ed041ea905e" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4363034/asante-samuel-jr">Asante Samuel Jr</a>., eventually leading to rookie <a data-player-guid="c4f37108-302c-3730-b2eb-a6926cdb02bc" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685327/daylen-everette">Daylen Everette</a> replacing Samuel in the fourth quarter. Big-bodied receivers <a data-player-guid="f6207352-946a-a75a-aff5-28f316536d4d" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4239993/tee-higgins">Tee Higgins</a> and <a data-player-guid="f9be91fa-7d8d-811b-6452-b14d1a1feb2c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4362628/jamarr-chase">Ja'Marr Chase</a> overpowered Samuel several times, including on Higgins' second-quarter touchdown, when the receiver boxed out the smaller Samuel. In the fourth quarter, the rookie was then part of a group responsible for a busted coverage that resulted in a <a data-player-guid="f3cc6528-0247-52b4-23c4-4c54da4e1571" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3116164/mike-gesicki">Mike Gesicki</a> touchdown.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> With <a data-player-guid="da1e8487-d66d-6ff0-7438-e9d6e77856e0" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4038815/rico-dowdle">Rico Dowdle</a> out, running back <a data-player-guid="224e4c1e-625d-b1b2-b8ea-1316942fa7ac" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4569987/jaylen-warren">Jaylen Warren</a> played more than 90% of the offensive snaps -- a far cry from the balanced workload he carried with Dowdle in the first two weeks. With 17 carries for 127 yards, he showed Sunday that he's more than capable of carrying the load. It wasn't a perfect afternoon for Warren, though, as he got tripped up on the turf yards away from a breakaway touchdown late in the fourth quarter. <em>-- Brooke Pryor</em></p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room: </strong>"It sucks that you have to have something like this happen after a loss," said LT <a data-player-guid="91893b7e-db5e-d0fa-5191-37e6df06b823" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4427170/troy-fautanu">Troy Fautanu</a> on the offense's bounce-back performance. "Obviously you want to do this regardless if you win the week before or not, but sometimes you got to get punched in the face in order to learn."</p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Browns (Thursday, 8:15 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50045667" data-cerebro-id="6ab980f44bf4c005207b9d1c" data-title="Steelers hit Burrow, recover fumble to seal win over Bengals" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04/dace1edc-2f36-4262-afa7-937681b72a04.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50045667">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:37</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Steelers hit Burrow, recover fumble to seal win over Bengals</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/cin.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Bengals</h2><p><strong>Are the Bengals playing well enough to be considered a serious contender?</strong> Sunday put a serious dent in that belief. After a good performance in all three phases against Houston, it was anything but that against the Steelers. Notably, the team had two bad special teams blunders -- a roughing the punter penalty and a muffed punt that ultimately led to 10 points. And Cincinnati's defense, while good in spots, gave up significant yardage after the catch, including on a late 47-yard reception by tight end <a data-player-guid="cc423765-e806-35e3-ae40-863502fa6122" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430802/darnell-washington">Darnell Washington</a>. The Steelers finished with 411 yards.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> It was good up until the end. Burrow probably tried to do a bit too much trying to extend a play late and coughed up the ball with the Bengals driving for a potential tie or win. He completed his first 14 passes of the game and threw three touchdown passes, including a key fourth-down conversion that kept Cincinnati's hopes of winning alive. <em>-- Ben Baby</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Jaguars (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Warren took on a volume role with Rico Dowdle out with a toe injury, scoring a season-high 20.6 fantasy points. If Dowdle has to sit again in Week 4, Warren can be played as a midtier RB2. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="tennyg"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872956">N.Y. Giants 12, Tennessee 7</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872956">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872956">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/nyg.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Giants</h2><p><strong>Did <a data-player-guid="57af2581-cec9-d5a3-2afe-7a719925f78b" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2969939/jameis-winston">Jameis Winston</a> do enough to inspire confidence as Giants QB?</strong> It wasn't perfect, but a win is a win. Winston did enough to help the Giants beat a struggling Titans team. His accuracy was off early, but he made some big plays throughout the game, especially on the opening drive of the second half. He finished 14-of-22 for 118 yards. It should be enough for him to remain the starter, and the Giants are still intent on adding another QB. <a data-player-guid="1d58c054-8e0e-1f6e-7267-02ec9679f43f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16760/jimmy-garoppolo">Jimmy Garoppolo</a>, <a data-player-guid="460fbf74-c64d-3862-b942-852d104e94dd" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4433970/jj-mccarthy">J.J. McCarthy</a> and Gardner Minshew are the most likely options.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Running back Najee Harris' role increases. The veteran had four carries in his debut last week and nine Sunday for 52 yards. Harris jump-started the Giants' offense with six carries for 36 yards on their first drive of the second half. It should increase his playing time and role moving forward. Starter <a data-player-guid="0be760c4-3eb7-338a-9b0b-20de5895543c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4696981/cam-skattebo">Cam Skattebo</a> had 23 touches for 100 yards.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room:</strong> "That was a great win," Skattebo said. "A year ago, we lose that game 100%." <em>-- Jordan Raanan</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Cardinals (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50045372" data-cerebro-id="6ab97cb175ba89659fc62cfc" data-title="Jevon Holland picks off Cam Ward to seal the win for the Giants" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8/45a66ec7-ab77-4b0a-a060-b3932bf04ab8.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50045372">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:47</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Jevon Holland picks off Cam Ward to seal the win for the Giants</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/ten.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Titans</h2><p><strong>Are the Titans playing like the worst team in the league?</strong> The Titans' offense was downright miserable for most of the game. Quarterback <a data-player-guid="9f4e87b5-5da8-38c0-9951-e3496b55b3c8" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4688380/cam-ward">Cam Ward</a> failed to see open receivers on multiple plays and missed <a data-player-guid="58f8add5-078d-3663-9249-0f48f77ce044" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4871023/carnell-tate">Carnell Tate</a> for what should have been an easy touchdown. They opened with five consecutive three-and-outs and finally got a first down late in the third quarter. The series of three-and-outs came after <a data-player-guid="570f2134-7526-3cea-ac53-012280ed5613" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431268/chimere-dike">Chimere Dike</a> fumbled the opening kickoff. It was a respectable effort by the defense, but Ward's inexplicable pass late in the fourth resulted in an interception and a Titans loss.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Time of possession was an issue for the third game. At one point, the Giants held a 28:15 to 9:49 edge. The Titans managed to drive 91 yards in seven minutes late in the fourth quarter for their first points to help cut the deficit in time of possession and the overall score. The final drive, which ended in an interception, made it 34:26 to 25:34. <em>-- Turron Davenport</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Ravens (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Giants WR <a data-player-guid="44a2174b-1d11-3acf-8e75-fe0c13db47a6" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4595348/malik-nabers">Malik Nabers</a> is struggling terribly with QB <a data-player-guid="13e97d3e-2171-371b-9a7a-2c44670b5a62" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4689114/jaxson-dart">Jaxson Dart</a> sidelined. Nabers' 7.6 fantasy points gives him two of the four worst fantasy scores of his career in the past two weeks. Nabers might have difficulty delivering even WR2 value without a QB upgrade. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="lacbuf"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872953">Buffalo 24, L.A. Chargers 16</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872953">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872953">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/buf.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Bills</h2><p><strong>How did the Bills remain undefeated after committing five turnovers?</strong> Five turnovers, 10 penalties, two dropped interceptions and four sacks allowed. Quarterback <a data-player-guid="237b9f2a-4701-8fc3-60eb-250978af9893" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3918298/josh-allen">Josh Allen</a>'s passer rating was barely north of 50. The Bills had no right to have kept this one close, but despite that the game never spun out of control. These battled-tested Bills somehow avoided spiraling or pressing. Give the defense its flowers, but the real impressive trend was the team's overall composure in the face of mistake after mistake to keep the win in reach.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> This was the first time the Bills won a game with a minus-four turnover differential since 1997. The opposing quarterback that afternoon was Chargers coach Jim Harbaugh. That was also the last time the Bills won any game in which they turned the ball over five times.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room: </strong>When asked if it felt like the Bills stole their win over the Chargers, Allen said it 100% did. "To be tied at halftime felt like a dream, to be honest," Allen said.<em> -- Nick Suss</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Patriots (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50044851" data-cerebro-id="6ab974fc75ba89659fc62864" data-title="Josh Allen's QB sneak give the Bills the lead" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35/c51eab2d-1f28-404e-8b16-18b4553daf35.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50044851">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:20</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Josh Allen's QB sneak give the Bills the lead</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/lac.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Chargers</h2><p><strong>How concerning is <a data-player-guid="ec880cbc-1490-cdae-548f-f844104974ae" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4038941/justin-herbert">Justin Herbert</a>'s start to the season?</strong> The defense tried its best to give Herbert and the offense a chance to win. Herbert -- who could have easily had three interceptions -- ended up throwing just one, and yet, the interception to C.J. Gardner-Johnson was a dagger. Herbert's play wasn't the only issue, as there were dropped passes and questionable playcalls. But ultimately, he hasn't looked like the superstar he was during the first six years of his career.</p><p><strong>Most surprising performance:</strong> The Chargers' defense. Five turnovers typically means a win in the NFL. Somehow, it didn't on this day. Nevertheless, putting a lid on the league's best offense was encouraging. This is a unit that struggled against Raiders quarterback <a data-player-guid="53bec012-c2ed-bc7c-a8d5-438611f9faa1" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/14880/kirk-cousins">Kirk Cousins</a> and Cardinals quarterback Jacoby Brissett. So the Chargers should feel encouraged that their defense -- which has been the top unit the past two seasons -- is back. <em>-- Kris Rhim</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Seahawks (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Is Chargers RB Omarion Hampton's grip on the primary running back role no longer ironclad? He barely edged <a data-player-guid="d1faa993-e3a2-38bb-9c84-8f7e017c155c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4596334/keaton-mitchell">Keaton Mitchell</a> in snap share (42% to 36%) and total touches (15 to 11). Mitchell also had the better underlying metrics, hinting at more sharing moving forward. Add Mitchell, who is available in 84.4% of ESPN leagues. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="houind"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872951">Indianapolis 19, Houston 17</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872951">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872951">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/ind.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Colts</h2><p><strong>Has the Colts' defense stopped the bleeding?</strong> The Colts entered this game ranked last in several major defensive categories, including a staggering 1,029 yards allowed in the first two weeks -- second most in NFL history. On Sunday, the missed assignments that led to wide-open receivers in the first two games and the flurry of missed tackles seemed to be mostly addressed. The Colts also took advantage of Houston's porous pass protection to consistently pressure Texans QB <a data-player-guid="147e6862-2ac0-3a97-8f36-e3b1c0147320" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432577/cj-stroud">C.J. Stroud</a>. Whether this was a one-week reprieve or the start of a trend, the Colts needed this.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> <a data-player-guid="5ad1bcc2-57bc-bb72-bcd0-0cdd0d945444" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917792/daniel-jones">Daniel Jones</a> did not play smart in this game, as at least two of his three turnovers could be attributed to his own decisions. Jones' interception came when he threw a desperation pass while under pressure in field goal range. He also fumbled in the fourth quarter after not protecting the ball despite having multiple pass rushers converging on him. He did make some clutch throws on the game-winning drive. <em>-- Stephen Holder</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Commanders in London (Sunday, 9:30 a.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50043788" data-cerebro-id="6ab95a5b4bf4c005207b8984" data-title="Keenan Allen scores his first TD as a Colt" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0/320eadf0-48ef-4eb7-8323-16fecfd441e0.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50043788">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:20</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Keenan Allen scores his first TD as a Colt</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/hou.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Texans</h2><p><strong>Is it time to panic on the Texans' 2026 season?</strong> It's trending that way. Even though the Texans' defense forced three turnovers (two in the second half) and had clutch plays from Stroud on their second-to-last drive to take the lead, it wasn't enough. Yes, the Texans started 0-3 last season and recovered, but that is not sustainable again. No team in NFL history has ever overcome 0-3 starts in back-to-back seasons, so expecting Houston to do that again is unrealistic.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Houston's defense had zero turnovers coming into Week 3, but forced three, which gave them a chance to win. That's the type of playmaking defense Houston wants. And they're going to need it to dig themselves out of this hole. <em>-- DJ Bien-Aime</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> vs. Cowboys (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Colts WR <a data-player-guid="c22ef201-95ad-1740-dd33-3ae06d7e7e68" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15818/keenan-allen">Keenan Allen</a> scored 18.3 fantasy points, stepping up as a short-route target over the middle while <a data-player-guid="b6d37bf2-1fa1-1415-1323-5506b68a7206" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360078/alec-pierce">Alec Pierce</a> (heel) heals. Daniel Jones' area of strength has come in the short game so far this season, so Allen shapes up as a matchup-dependent fantasy WR3 in the short term. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="nyjdet"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872954">Detroit 31, N.Y. Jets 24</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872954">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872954">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/det.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Lions</h2><p><strong>Have the Lions fixed their defensive issues after rough start to season?</strong> After giving up 71 points through the first two weeks, Detroit shook up its secondary with <a data-player-guid="eed68b14-8f0d-e66c-e0b1-23caf24c7cf9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3910229/rock-ya-sin">Rock Ya-Sin</a> serving a reserve role, while CB <a data-player-guid="94aa18de-e04a-ae52-6e23-3f72ffce1141" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4371973/roger-mccreary">Roger McCreary</a> started at outside cornerback alongside veteran <a data-player-guid="9d4fc11f-597a-9b5b-d095-4d91e1aae783" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3139387/dj-reed">D.J. Reed</a>. Entering the game, the Lions were outgained by 191 total yards, fifth worst in the NFL, but second-year defensive coordinator Kelvin Sheppard refused to do any finger-pointing. Instead, he held a Monday meeting to dissect the struggles. The unit responded with a key takeaway in crunch time, but the defense still has major work to do.</p><p><strong>Key stat to know:</strong> <a data-player-guid="d85aed19-e3b8-3788-935e-55f636ad86e9" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429795/jahmyr-gibbs">Jahmyr Gibbs</a> finished with three total TDs, but his two rushing touchdowns helped him surpass Billy Sims (42) for the second-most rushing TDs (43) in franchise history -- trailing only Barry Sanders (99). Sanders was in attendance as part of the Lions' alumni homecoming. Gibbs put on a show in front of the Hall of Famer, finishing with 20 carries for 99 rushing yards and seven catches for 65 receiving yards. <em>-- Eric Woodyard</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Panthers (Sunday, 8:20 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50044472" data-cerebro-id="6ab96de34bf4c005207b924d" data-title="Jahmyr Gibbs punches in for his second TD of the game" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e/e2244e1d-dbca-468d-8b1c-d6f9dc8ba90e.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50044472">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:28</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Jahmyr Gibbs punches in for his second TD of the game</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/nyj.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Jets</h2><p><strong>Why can't the Jets win close games?</strong> Another week, another crushing loss. The Jets had a chance to steal one in Motown, but their defense -- ranked No. 1 in yards allowed heading into the game -- imploded in crunch time. They let the Lions march 65 yards on four plays for the winning touchdown with 2:20 left in the fourth quarter, thanks to blown coverages on two pass plays. Then QB <a data-player-guid="593e3c58-2b92-e0f1-f4a8-84215e27f023" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15864/geno-smith">Geno Smith</a> fumbled on the ensuing possession. Good teams rise up in the clutch; the Jets haven't mastered that yet. They blew a 10-point lead last week and lost in overtime. This week, a 14-point comeback wasn't enough.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Rookie TE <a data-player-guid="51be0cd2-da0c-360f-be3e-62ba52957c83" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5083315/kenyon-sadiq">Kenyon Sadiq</a> has arrived. It took only three games for the first-round pick to establish himself as a versatile target. He caught seven passes for 105 yards, including a 24-yard touchdown on a diving play in the end zone. Sadiq now has a receiving TD and a rushing TD (Week 1) in his first three games.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room:</strong> Aaron Glenn on his close relationship with Dan Campbell: "I love him to death, I do. He's a huge part of how I've grown in this league. But this was a tough one for us. This is a tough one." <em>-- Rich Cimini</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Bears (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Sadiq displayed his seam-stretching ability in a positive matchup versus the Lions' secondary, scoring a career-best 23.5 points. Available in over 65% of ESPN leagues, he should be added this week. But Sadiq should still be viewed only as a deeper league starter. <em>-- Bowen</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="nejax"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872957">Jacksonville 35, New England 6</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872957">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872957">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/jax.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Jaguars</h2><p><strong>Do the Jaguars even need <a data-player-guid="c39cf8be-f94e-3db4-9c3a-fcc72135a03f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685415/travis-hunter">Travis Hunter</a> to play offense?</strong> After three weeks, Hunter has one catch and one carry. He hasn't touched the ball on offense since the opener. Hunter played five offensive snaps Sunday, giving him 16 for the season. But the Jaguars have scored 82 points, rookie WR <a data-player-guid="a5aacdd7-7efb-3132-8972-3f3677368741" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4879194/josh-cameron">Josh Cameron</a> has emerged, and QB <a data-player-guid="76111495-d1d9-2333-170d-4206eebe673f" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360310/trevor-lawrence">Trevor Lawrence</a> is having success spreading the ball around. The run game cranked up against New England, too (135 yards). Why force Hunter on the field if the offense is rolling without him?</p><p><strong>Most surprising performance:</strong> The Jaguars gave Cameron a bigger role in Week 3, and he delivered with a touchdown catch (second on three catches this season) and a 42-yard kickoff return. Through three quarters versus the Patriots, he had nearly as many snaps on offense (16) as <a data-player-guid="f7b37472-30a8-395c-8ade-5462fbda15d4" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432773/brian-thomas-jr">Brian Thomas Jr</a>. (21) -- an indication that more work could be ahead as the season progresses.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room: </strong>Hunter on his end zone interception: "I know [Maye] tried me a couple times, so I was just in there saying, 'I'm getting too close to the ball. I got to get me one.' So we just continued to just do what the coaches schemed up for us and we just played our best part of it." <em>-- Michael DiRocco</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Bengals (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50044549" data-cerebro-id="6ab96f8a75ba89659fc62723" data-title="Jarrian Jones picks off Drake Maye to set up a Chris Rodriguez Jr. TD" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2/f8867e0d-5eba-4a26-a93c-5d50a599fba2.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50044549">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:19</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Jarrian Jones picks off Drake Maye to set up a Chris Rodriguez Jr. TD</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/ne.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Patriots</h2><p><strong>What can the Patriots do to get <a data-player-guid="2fbd2f9e-624d-3e63-9bb5-9bb965782b68" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431452/drake-maye">Drake Maye</a> back on track?</strong> Maye's 2026 woes continued with his 10th game of multiple turnovers (tied for most in NFL since 2024). The end zone interception just before halftime, on third-and-goal from the 2-yard line, was a shocking decision as WR <a data-player-guid="c10735fc-cc78-3252-b11a-525d9cb0298e" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4695193/efton-chism">Efton Chism III</a> was tightly covered by Travis Hunter. It was a play similar to Maye's miscue in the season-opening loss at Seattle. In the first half, Maye was pressured 11 times -- his most before halftime in his career -- and went 2-of-7 with an interception and two sacks, per ESPN Research.</p><p><strong>Trend to watch:</strong> Offensive line injuries. Veteran <a data-player-guid="a7ddea19-5b4b-10bf-d3d5-f2e5f900936c" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15718/greg-van-roten">Greg Van Roten</a>, who started at right guard in place of <a data-player-guid="44a779a5-c59c-bc8a-bb5f-c1e03b12aa76" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4046545/mike-onwenu">Mike Onwenu</a> (broken ankle), didn't return after leaving the game in the second quarter (thigh). <a data-player-guid="7d4560cb-9e1c-b8df-4e81-17e5e6963a70" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4428394/walter-rouse">Walter Rouse</a>, who was acquired in a trade with the Vikings in August, took over for Van Roten.</p><p><strong>Best quote from the locker room:</strong> Maye on the biggest difference from last season: "I think it's getting out of my own way. These mistakes that I'm making personally are really [not] them beating us, it's me beating myself. ... This league will humble you quick."<em> -- Mike Reiss</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Bills (Sunday, 1 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Though <a data-player-guid="6e206853-654e-64b6-48fb-544f0353705e" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4362619/chris-rodriguez-jr">Chris Rodriguez Jr</a>. scored, <a data-player-guid="7c6344a7-ae7c-372e-8337-ed04ccb56cc0" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4882093/bhayshul-tuten">Bhayshul Tuten</a> continued to flash his elite speed, scoring 17.0 fantasy points on 17 touches. Tuten's 48% snap share and usage offer encouragement that he can be a weekly fantasy RB2. (And, for what it's worth, sit Maye next week at Buffalo. Please.) <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p><img src="https://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png" width="100%"><p><a name="kcmia"></a></p><h2><a href="/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872952">Kansas City 24, Miami 10</a></h2><p><strong>Catch up on the action:</strong> <a href="/nfl/boxscore/_/gameId/401872952">Box score</a> | <a href="/nfl/recap/_/gameId/401872952">Recap</a></p><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/kc.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Chiefs</h2><p><strong>Despite winning, should the Chiefs be concerned about their pass rush?</strong> Entering Week 3, no NFL QB had been sacked more than Dolphins quarterback <a data-player-guid="77d56116-fed8-b61e-d8d8-9a30107e2104" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4242512/malik-willis">Malik Willis</a> (nine). The fact that the Chiefs couldn't pressure him while not blitzing was similar to the pass-rush struggles of last season, when defensive tackle <a data-player-guid="3a9adacc-63fb-4f5e-805d-d98750056eef" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3044859/chris-jones">Chris Jones</a> was the lone major presence. On Sunday, defensive end <a data-player-guid="5c6a6d9e-f116-c17f-3e30-23accba436db" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426659/george-karlaftis">George Karlaftis</a> was the lone defender to record a hit on Willis. The Chiefs won't beat better opponents with a similar performance. The Chiefs also didn't sack Colts quarterback <a data-player-guid="5ad1bcc2-57bc-bb72-bcd0-0cdd0d945444" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917792/daniel-jones">Daniel Jones</a> last week -- and that game ended in overtime.</p><p><strong>Stat to know:</strong> Running back <a data-player-guid="c0a76b7f-7b5d-be73-5e81-258439651478" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4567048/kenneth-walker">Kenneth Walker III</a> is the first player to have two games with a rushing and receiving touchdown within his team's first three games of a season since 2017, when former running back <a data-player-guid="7241840c-3e99-0a3a-f370-d0faa5033632" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2977644/todd-gurley">Todd Gurley</a> was a member of the Rams. Walker is also the first player in Chiefs history to accomplish the feat. <em>-- Nate Taylor</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Raiders (Sunday, 4:25 p.m. ET)</p><div data-behavior="video_scroll" class="contentItem__content contentItem__content--media-card contentItem__content--fullWidth contentItem__content--inline"><figure  data-video="watch,640,360,50043719" data-cerebro-id="6ab957b84bf4c005207b8879" data-title="Patrick Mahomes shovels it to Kenneth Walker III for his 2nd TD of the game" class="media-wrapper_image video" data-source="espn" data-contributing-partner="wsc"><picture  class="media-wrapper_image" ><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156.jpg" media="(min-width: 376px)"><source data-srcset="https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156.jpg, https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/wsc/2026/0927/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156/686db305-f754-44c6-971b-5cba5a2fa156.jpg 2x" media="(max-width: 375px)"><img  class=" lazyload lazyload"  ></picture><span class="video-play-button" data-id="50043719">play</span><figcaption class="media-caption"><div class="media-duration">0:23</div></figcaption></figure><div class="contentItem__contentWrapper"><div class="contentItem__title contentItem__title--media">Patrick Mahomes shovels it to Kenneth Walker III for his 2nd TD of the game</div></div></div><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/mia.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><h2>Dolphins</h2><div class="ad-300"><div class="ad-center"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-incontent2 ad-wrapper" data-slot-type="incontent2" data-slot-kvps="pos=incontent2" data-independent="true"></div></div></div><p><strong>Have the Dolphins begun to turn the page on both sides of the ball?</strong> On defense, absolutely. The Dolphins kept the game in front of them, forced turnovers and rallied after an ugly first two drives. Linebacker <a data-player-guid="abc2a40f-e66c-34b4-b2cd-50794b39d122" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4566094/jacob-rodriguez">Jacob Rodriguez</a> recorded his first career takeaway and looked like a future star. The Chiefs' offense made plenty of mistakes, but Miami flew to the ball and limited explosives for the most part. Meanwhile, the Dolphins' passing game looked sharper than it has all season, but they struggled to run the ball after <a data-player-guid="ce7195db-c46d-3963-a973-2fadf206a70b" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429160/devon-achane">De'Von Achane</a> was <a href="/nfl/story/_/id/50044229/dolphins-rb-devon-achane-suffers-knee-injury-vs-chiefs">injured</a> on the opening drive. We will see if Miami can build on this next week.</p><p><strong>What to make of the QB performance:</strong> Willis completed 20 of 36 passes for 210 yards in possibly his best performance of the season. Unlike his previous two games, Willis made quicker decisions with the football and was far more willing to take off if receivers weren't open. That being said, his accuracy waned at times, and he missed a few deep shots. <em>-- Marcel Louis-Jacques</em></p><p><strong>Next game:</strong> at Vikings (Sunday, 4:05 p.m. ET)</p><hr><img alt="" class="floatleft" src="https://g.espncdn.com/lm-static/ffl/images/ffl-shield-icon-500.png?w=110&h=110&transparent=true" width="31"><p><strong>Fantasy football takeaway:</strong> Dolphins RB <a data-player-guid="47d181c5-f3aa-37fb-8f46-5305d4977f12" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4711533/ollie-gordon-ii">Ollie Gordon II</a> played 83% of the offensive snaps after Achane's injury, recording 20 touches and 14.5 fantasy points. The Dolphins would probably activate <a data-player-guid="3d605ae2-3f59-3250-8fe2-b2df5d9d64c4" href="https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4682745/jaylen-wright">Jaylen Wright</a> for depth next week, but Gordon should be a priority pickup if Achane's prognosis for Week 4 is iffy. <em>-- Cockcroft</em></p>
</div><footer class="article-footer" data-behavior="footer_region"><div class="sponsored-links"><div class="sponsored-headlines"><div class="taboola-container" data-network="espn-network" data-src="https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50043408/week-3-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026" data-type="story" data-mode="thumbnails-3x1-a" data-placement="story - nfl" data-target-type="mix" data-container="taboola-story---sport"></div></div></div>
